Architecture plan for issues #89-#90

Project shape
- Static browser-only camera capture app using plain HTML, CSS, and ES modules.
- Runtime modules live in `js/`; gallery rendering is isolated in `js/gallery.js`.
- Tests use Vitest with DOM APIs from the configured test environment.
- Captures persist in browser `localStorage` as storage item records from `js/storage.js`.

Module structure and shared contracts
- Keep the stored item shape unchanged: video items continue to store `data:<mime>;base64,<payload>` in `item.data`.
- Add gallery-local helpers in `js/gallery.js` for video blob handling:
  - Parse data URLs into `{ mimeType, bytes }` without changing storage.
  - Build `Blob` instances from decoded `Uint8Array` payloads.
  - Create object URLs for rendered video cards with `URL.createObjectURL`.
  - Choose download extensions from the parsed MIME type, using `.webm` and `.mp4` for supported video types.
- Keep picture cards on existing data URLs so still-image behavior remains unchanged.
- Track object URLs created during each render and revoke them before replacement/re-render and when deleting cards, preventing leaked browser resources.

Issue dependencies
- #89 is the implementation issue and should land first. It changes runtime gallery rendering and cleanup behavior.
- #90 depends on #89. Its tests should assert the blob URL path for video cards, preserve picture data URL coverage, and verify cleanup via `URL.revokeObjectURL`.

Key design decisions
- Blob conversion belongs in `js/gallery.js` because it is a presentation/download concern, not a storage schema change.
- Avoid adding dependencies; use browser-native `atob`, `Uint8Array`, `Blob`, and `URL` APIs.
- Keep helper functions small and test through DOM behavior unless direct exports are already necessary.
- Gracefully fall back to existing data URLs if a video data URL is malformed, so one bad stored item does not break the whole gallery render.
- Tests should stub `URL.createObjectURL` and `URL.revokeObjectURL` deterministically and assert the created `Blob.type`.
